    "question": "The price of a home is $98 per square foot (sq ft).  The house is 2,400 sq ft and the barn out back is 1,000 sq ft.  How much is this property?",
    "gold": "333200",
    "answer": "The house is 2,400 sq ft and the barn is 1,000 sq ft so it's 2400+1000 = <<2400+1000=3400>>3,400 sq ft\nThe price is $98 per sq ft and it's 3,400 sq ft big so the property costs 98*3400 = $<<98*3400=333200.00>>333,200.00\n#### 333200"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total price of the property, we need to calculate the cost of the house and the barn separately, and then sum these costs.\n\nFirst, we calculate the cost of the house. The house is 2,400 square feet and the price per square foot is $98. Therefore, the cost of the house is:\n\\[\n2400 \\text{ sq ft} \\times 98 \\text{ dollars/sq ft} = 235200 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the cost of the barn. The barn is 1,000 square feet and the price per square foot is $98. Therefore, the cost of the barn is:\n\\[\n1000 \\text{ sq ft} \\times 98 \\text{ dollars/sq ft} = 98000 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the cost of the house and the cost of the barn to find the total price of the property:\n\\[\n235200 \\text{ dollars} + 98000 \\text{ dollars} = 333200 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nThus, the total price of the property is \\boxed{333200}.",
